# Neuromorphic Audio Wake-Word Detection
# Small SNN detects a wake word using spike-encoded audio features.
# Temporal coincidence detection with cochlear-inspired topology.

Define a network named audio_wakeword with timestep 0.0018.
# Network with 1 input, 3 LIF neurons, 3 linear transforms, 1 output.
# flow: input → sensor → interneuron → actuator → output
#        sensor ─────────────────────→ actuator

# Layers:
Define an input port named input with shape (1,).
Define a LIF neuron named sensor with time constant 0.005, resistance 1.0, leak voltage 0.0, and firing threshold 0.6.
Define a linear transformation named w_sensor_interneuron with weight matrix shape (45, 1) annotated with metadata weight_init equal to "xavier" annotated with metadata seed equal to 42.
Define a LIF neuron named interneuron with time constant 0.01, resistance 1.0, leak voltage 0.0, and firing threshold 0.55.
Define a linear transformation named w_interneuron_actuator with weight matrix shape (1, 45) annotated with metadata weight_init equal to "xavier" annotated with metadata seed equal to 43.
Define a linear transformation named w_sensor_actuator with weight matrix shape (1, 1) annotated with metadata weight_init equal to "xavier" annotated with metadata seed equal to 44.
Define a LIF neuron named actuator with time constant 0.02, resistance 1.0, leak voltage 0.0, and firing threshold 0.9.
Define an output port named output with shape (1,).

# Connections:
input connects to sensor.
sensor connects to w_sensor_interneuron.
w_sensor_interneuron connects to interneuron.
interneuron connects to w_interneuron_actuator.
w_interneuron_actuator connects to actuator.
sensor connects to w_sensor_actuator.
w_sensor_actuator connects to actuator.
actuator connects to output.

# Note: axonal delays (5 ms, 8 ms) and STDP are dropped — not representable in NIR.
# Future extension: add delay and plasticity metadata layers.
